    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.map_smul_of_scaling: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:230-233 assumes “IsTempered μ”, “IsSpectralMeasure Γ μ”, “SpectralHomogeneous Γ (d-alpha)” and c>0; the conclusion is μ.map(c·)=ofReal(c^(-alpha))•μ. Ledger:1648 and claims.yaml:4105 agree. Main TeX:704-705 derives μ(cA)=c^αμ(A) from covariance scaling and Fourier uniqueness; :4522-4525 explicitly gives μ(A/c)=c^(-α)μ(A). This is the same pushforward statement, with a disclosed weaker assumption set."
