      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:325 defines “Real.exp 1 * MGamma Γ / (2 * Real.sqrt Real.pi)^d”, matching ledger:1652 and claims.yaml:4133. TeX:38 defines “e M_Γ/(2√π)^d”. There is no changed normalization or additional hypothesis."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.integrable_gauss_zero: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:329-330 assumes “IsTempered ν” and “0 < c” and concludes centered-Gaussian integrability, matching ledger:1653 and claims.yaml:4140. TeX:23-30 asserts Schwartz integrability in unlabelled prose; this separately named centered specialization is correctly classified as a Lean auxiliary."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.MGamma_pos: P:masked-spectral-growth",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:335-336 assumes “IsTempered Γ” and “Γ ≠ 0” and concludes both Gaussian integrability and “0 < MGamma Γ”, matching ledger:1654 and claims.yaml:4147. TeX:55-56 explicitly attributes finiteness to temperedness and positivity to Γ≠0. These are exactly the used hypotheses; finiteness is not inferred merely from a totalized real integral."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.gauss_const_cancel: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:345-346 assumes “0 < r” and states the exact constant-cancellation identity in ledger:1655 and claims.yaml:4154. TeX:40 assumes r>0 and :62-63 gives the reciprocal Fourier factor, but contains no separately stated cancellation lemma. The auxiliary classification is suitable."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.masked_gaussian_transform: E:masked-gaussian-transform",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:358-363 assumes “IsSpectralMeasure Γ μ” and “0 < r”, with arbitrary y, and gives the factor “(r/(2√π))^d” and phase exp(-i⟨y,x⟩). Ledger:1656 and claims.yaml:4161 match TeX:40-45 exactly. The ledger explicitly says this standalone generalized identity has no integrability conclusion; the paper wrapper proves integrability under the manuscript assumptions."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.translated_gauss_le: E:masked-translated-ball",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:383-386 assumes the spectral convention, “SpectralHomogeneous Γ (d-alpha)” and r>0, and bounds the integral by “r^alpha * MGamma Γ/(2√π)^d”. Ledger:1657 and claims.yaml:4168 agree. TeX:46-47 has the identical bound, derived from nonnegativity and Γ scaling at :67-74. The weaker standalone hypotheses and absence of integrability are explicitly disclosed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.closedBall_le: E:masked-translated-ball",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:421-424 adds “hint : Integrable … μ” to the spectral convention, Γ scaling and r>0, concluding the closed-ball bound in ENNReal. Ledger:1658 and claims.yaml:4175 reflect this. TeX:48-51 permits closed balls; its temperedness assumptions ensure Gaussian integrability (:23-30). Thus the explicit integrability condition is discharged under the manuscript hypotheses, not supplied externally."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.masked_spectral_growth: P:masked-spectral-growth",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:460-476 assumes Γ and μ tempered, the spectral convention, Γ scaling and Γ≠0. It concludes integrability, M_Γ>0, the transform, the nonnegative Gaussian bound and both ball bounds for “∀ y … ∀ r … 0 < r”. Ledger:1659 and claims.yaml:4182 preserve these conclusions. TeX:5-6,34-51 supplies the stronger standing assumptions and identical constants; the generalization is expressly identified."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.MaskedSpectralGrowth.masked_spectral_growth_paper: P:masked-spectral-growth",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:501-517 assumes only “HomogCovariance d alpha alpha0 Γ μ” and “Γ ≠ 0”. TeX:5-6 assumes H:homog and Γ≠0, and :34-51 states exactly its conclusions. Ledger:1660 and claims.yaml:4189 agree. All y∈ℝ^d and r>0, both ball conventions, both integrability conclusions, strict M_Γ positivity and the constants are retained."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.ClockCopyHomog.clock_copy_obstruction_paper: P:clock-copy-obstruction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "ClockCopyHomog.lean:53-66 assumes H:homog, Γ≠0, θ>0 and “-1 ≤ ρ ∧ ρ ≤ 1”, with no homogeneity argument. Main TeX:7514-7515,7531-7539 specifies the same covariance and parameter class; :7555-7575 states the matching positive integrable weight, exact identities, strict inequality and factor 2-2^a. Ledger:1661 and claims.yaml:4197 are faithful. The discharged input follows solely from H:homog at MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:315-317."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.ClockCopyHomog.damped_N2_nonneg_paper: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "ClockCopyHomog.lean:71-73 assumes “HomogCovariance …” and “0 < θ”, without Γ≠0 or a supplied spectral-homogeneity argument, and concludes “0 ≤ N2sq alpha0 θ μ”. Main TeX:677-679 states the same nonnegativity under H:homog for every θ>0. Ledger:1662 and claims.yaml:4204 match. The alternative proof route is disclosed rather than attributed to the TeX's temporal-positive-definiteness argument."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.ClockCopyHomog.damped_norms_finite_paper: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "ClockCopyHomog.lean:80-86 assumes only H:homog and θ>0 and concludes absolute integrability of the N₂ triple integrand, its outer integrand and the N₁ Laplace integrand. Main TeX:677-679 asserts finiteness under exactly those hypotheses, with absolute integration justified at :714-729. Ledger:1663 and claims.yaml:4211 accurately restrict the scope to N₁,N₂ finiteness; N₀, scaling, tails and smoothing are not claimed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-MaskedSpectralGrowth",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:1525-1621 accurately describes the three modules, manuscript locations, generalized hypotheses, unused carried fields, totalized integrals, integrability conclusions and alternative uniqueness route. MaskedSpectralGrowth.lean:230-317 derives spectral homogeneity without an external input. The α=0 examples are explicitly confined to variants of general theorems (:1609-1614), consistent with H:homog excluding α=0. The stated omissions are appropriately bounded."
    },
    {
      "claim": "LEDGER-INDEX",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "W2: Ledger:213-220 contains all 39 distinct declarations, and all cited section labels exist in the manuscript. However, the L:low-alpha-convolution index row at :217 lists only spectralHomogeneous_of_scaling, while declaration rows :1648 and :1650 also assign map_smul_of_scaling and spectralHomogeneous_of_homog to that label. Therefore the index does not reproduce exactly the label associations given by the section's rows."
    },
    {
      "claim": "COVERAGE-ROWS",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "coverage.yaml:70-88 correctly classifies L:damped-homogeneous-norms as same-assumptions/weaker and explicitly excludes N₀, scaling, tails and smoothing. Its :359-382 clock-copy row is same-assumptions/full and includes the new no-input wrapper. Its :439-456 masked-growth row is same-assumptions/full. The relevant claim IDs resolve in claims.yaml:3939-4214, and the new wrappers justify the classifications without silently retaining an extra hypothesis."
    },
    {
      "claim": "CROSS-REFERENCES",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Scope:61-68, ClockCopy introduction:654-665, and rows :802,837-838 explicitly distinguish the original wrappers' homogeneity argument from its now-proved discharge and the ClockCopyHomog wrappers. Not-in-Lean:2235-2238 correctly says spectral homogeneity is derived. FrequencyRow:1117-1120 says masked growth is not in that module, not that it is absent from Lean; :2240-2243 correctly distinguishes the unstated combined instance from its formalized inputs. No false remaining external-input claim was found in these cross-references."
    }
